FINDINGS:
1. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:2190 — `import` trailing `STORE` binds the alias via `bind`/`set_var`, which inside `module_depth > 0` lands in the module's own scope (src/bytecode/vm.rs:810), while the tree-walker binds the same name via `bind_module_name` into `globals` (src/vm.rs:719) — an `import json as J` inside `module M … end` is lost when the module scope pops on one VM and persists on the other — concrete fix: bind the alias through the globals path when handling `IMPORT`/`STORE`, not through `set_var`.
2. [MAJOR] src/bytecode/vm.rs:832 — `declare_const` inserts unconditionally into `globals`, ignoring `module_depth`, while `declare_member` (src/bytecode/vm.rs:2328) reads only `locals` — `module M` with `constant X to 1` plus `export X` passes validation (`module_declared_names` includes it) then `finish_module` silently publishes nothing — concrete fix: bind `constant` into the module scope like `set_var` does, or refuse/lookup globals in `declare_member`.
3. [MAJOR] src/parser.rs:267 — `module_body` returns the single `Module` body when exactly one declaration exists and the whole program otherwise, so top-level siblings beside a `module` declaration are dropped when a file is read as a module, and a two-module file takes yet another path — no test covers either side — concrete fix: define and pin sibling/two-module behavior or refuse it with a spanned error.
4. [MINOR] src/formatter.rs:440 — writes `" to "` for an import alias while `SPEC.md`/`docs/GRAMMAR.md` and `src/parser.rs:575` document `as` as the spelling, so `rb format` rewrites `import json as J` to `import json to J` — concrete fix: emit `as` and update the two pinned `to` fixtures.
REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
